& [SJS]
  + Situation: typed custody queries are operational but callers lack a governed way to obtain candidate handles
  + Justification: bounded exact metadata filtering closes the bootstrap gap without opening persistence semantic ranking or full-state disclosure
  + Solution: filter deterministic registry handles through a strict selector and return digest-bound body-free discovery results

& [Delineation]
  + bootstrap identifies the supplied registry snapshot and not external provenance or freshness
  + root-pinned queries prevent silent snapshot substitution after bootstrap
  + structural filters are not semantic term association or neural correlation
  + returned handles still require exact custody for resolution or resume

& [DataDrivenDesign]
  + BTreeMap iteration fixes digest-key order
  + optional fields combine as logical AND and maximum results bounds output
  + selector and response digests bind complete strict values
  + available versus returned counts plus truncation preserve pagination meaning

& [FacultyReview]
  + Honesty names bootstrap pinned structural and semantic-search boundaries separately
  + Security validates roots selector shape order exact handles entry digests counts and body denials
  + Planner maps explicit filter combinations to a bounded result set
  + Weaver joins discovery handles to the already proven custody query seam
  + Scribe records selector response and snapshot identities
  + Refiner returns only handle metadata and applies result bounds
  + Observer compares discovered entries with direct registry filtering and mutation cases

& [Decision]
  + activate isolated handle discovery forms dispatch serializer bounded CLI and adversarial tests
  + keep semantic correlation persistent catalogue and live provider integration outside authority

& [Rollback]
  + additive module CLI branch exports and tests remove without changing the Slice7E release candidate
